{
 "_comment": "RAD20: end-to-end A/B of the helper lane threads sleeping in GPU completion events (RAD20 build) against the parent commit's yield-polling lanes (baseline build), working Flash-Next layout (R9700 engine + two XTX helpers). The arms differ only in the build their r3_moe_worker comes from (the harness takes the helper from <binary>/../radiance_home); the engine kernels come from the baseline build's RAD_HOME in both. Combine off in both. Needs the feat/rad20-blocking-lanes helper build; kept as the RAD20 record. Set RAD_BIN_BASE, RAD_BIN_NEW, RAD_HOME and R9700_BDF before use (tools/lab/radiance/rad20-rad18-e2e.sh does).",
 "schema_version": 1,
 "engine": "radiance",
 "evidence_role": "diagnostic",
